SPP1 T-Deck differential -- 2026-10-14
baseline: C:/Dev/uvw-spp1-base @ e089f2c5 (build-probe); SPP1: C:/Dev/ultima-v-native-parity @ c4f53082 + the A11 latch fix (build-spp1)
packs (both runs): native/assets/openu5-alpha1-resources.bin 85b38994eea674e4..., openu5-audio.bin 28c1533b7b061da1...

FIRST RUN (before the A11 fix, same baseline): the classifier's precursor flagged six conversation walks
(T-0-3, T-0-4, T-0-5, T-1-4, T-1-5, T-2-4) whose first divergence was the RET that ENDS a town
conversation, with the SPP1 build one turn ahead (e.g. T-0-3 step 7: base turns=0 clock 5:09:00,
SPP1 turns=1 clock 5:09:01; text, mode and prompt identical). Cause: the device asks "Your interest?"
in TextEntry with request Dialogue and never enters UiMode::Dialogue, so settle_dispatcher_turn's
"a conversation runs on its own loop's time" latch never fired. Unexpected (TALK's nonzero return is
unresolved, so SPP1 must not change a conversation's cost) -> fixed: the latch also reads
dialogue_.active; spp1_runtime A11 (RED before, GREEN after, both profiles) and mutant A8 pin it.
In the rerun below those walks diverge later, at a cancelled town Jimmy / X-it (A), as expected.

